<p>
I am experimenting with involving subagents more in my LLM coding agent
workflow. I discovered that subagents make it more difficult to diagnose token
usage in Claude Code,
because the regular <code>/context</code> command only breaks down context usage for the
main conversation, not for the subagents.
</p>



<p>
I tried some existing tools like <code>ccusage</code> and <code>claude-agent-ledger</code>, but they
weren&rsquo;t able to give me the sort of breakdown into specifics I needed to
optimise my usage. Thus, I shamelessly had Claude Code whip up a tool that gives
me a better view of its token usage. This is vibecoded in the true sense of the
word – I have barely looked at the code – but I&rsquo;m okay with that becuase it is
not critical infrastructure and it does what I need it to.
</p>



